# Warp is cast from the hand only (CR 702.185a: "You may cast this card from your hand for its warp cost"), so a rule
# that lets a card be cast from another zone does not open it, though it opens an alternative cost that names no zone
# (CR 118.9, 601.3; Force of Will's, web-slinging's). Bot1 casts Pinnacle Emissary for its mana cost on turn 1 and Bot2
# bolts it. On turn 3 Bot1 casts Yawgmoth's Will ("you may cast spells from your graveyard"); with Mox Sapphire and Black
# Lotus up, the warp cost {U/R} could be paid, but the Emissary is in the graveyard, so warp is not offered (refused). It
# is cast from the graveyard for its mana cost {1}{U}{R} instead (the positive control), and, not warped, it is not
# exiled at the end step: it is still on the battlefield on turn 4. Black Lotus, sacrificed while the Will applies, and
# the Will itself are exiled.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Pinnacle Emissary
Swamp
Yawgmoth's Will
Black Lotus
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x18

